Feature: Outbound FIA Table Schema and Data Update for DELETE_FLAG

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks" and schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the following source tables exist:
      | source_table                  | clone_table                       |
      | ods_free_drug                 | ods_free_drug_clone               |
      | ods_non_contracting           | ods_non_contracting_clone         |
      | ods_copay                     | ods_copay_clone                   |
    And the source tables have a column "Filler_1" of type string, nullable

  Scenario Outline: Clone table creation with DELETE_FLAG NOT NULL and filtered data
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" exists
    When the clone table "<clone_table>" is dropped
    And the source table "<source_table>" is read
    And only rows where "Filler_1" IS NOT NULL are selected
    And the column "Filler_1" is renamed to "DELETE_FLAG"
    And the clone table "<clone_table>" is created as a Delta table with schema:
      | column_name      | type    | nullability |
      | <col1>           | <type1> | <null1>     |
      | <col2>           | <type2> | <null2>     |
      | <col3>           | <type3> | <null3>     |
      | DELETE_FLAG      | string  | NOT NULL    |
      | <col4>           | <type4> | <null4>     |
      | <col5>           | <type5> | <null5>     |
      | <col6>           | <type6> | <null6>     |
    Then the clone table "<clone_table>" contains only rows where "DELETE_FLAG" IS NOT NULL
    And the column "DELETE_FLAG" is present and defined as NOT NULL in the DDL
    And all other columns retain their original names, types, and nullability

    Examples:
      | source_table        | clone_table                | col1         | type1  | null1    | col2           | type2  | null2    | col3         | type3  | null3    | col4         | type4  | null4    | col5         | type5  | null5    | col6         | type6  | null6    |
      | ods_free_drug       | ods_free_drug_clone        | PM_ID        | string | nullable | Shipment_Date  | string | nullable | Dispense_ID  | bigint | nullable | Drug_Name    | string | nullable | Quantity     | bigint | nullable | Patient_ID   | string | nullable |
      | ods_non_contracting | ods_non_contracting_clone  | PM_ID        | string | nullable | Shipment_Date  | string | nullable | Dispense_ID  | bigint | nullable | Facility     | string | nullable | Units_Provided| bigint | nullable | Contract_Flag| string | nullable |
      | ods_copay           | ods_copay_clone            | PM_ID        | string | nullable | NDC            | string | nullable | Date_of_Service| string | nullable | Rx_Claim_Number| string | nullable | Copay_Amount | bigint | nullable | Plan_ID      | string | nullable |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Source table missing Filler_1 column
    Given the source table "<source_table>" does not have a column "Filler_1"
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then an error is raised with message "Source table <source_table> missing required column 'Filler_1'"

    Examples:
      | source_table        |
      | ods_free_drug       |
      | ods_non_contracting |
      | ods_copay           |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Filler_1 column type mismatch
    Given the source table "<source_table>" has column "Filler_1" of type <actual_type>
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then an error is raised with message "Column 'Filler_1' in <source_table> must be of type string, found <actual_type>"

    Examples:
      | source_table        | actual_type |
      | ods_free_drug       | bigint      |
      | ods_non_contracting | int         |
      | ods_copay           | boolean     |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Attempt to insert NULL into DELETE_FLAG
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" is created with DELETE_FLAG as NOT NULL
    When a row with DELETE_FLAG = NULL is inserted
    Then an error is raised with message "NOT NULL constraint failed for column 'DELETE_FLAG' in <clone_table>"

    Examples:
      | clone_table                |
      | ods_free_drug_clone        |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone  |
      | ods_copay_clone            |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Duplicate rows in source table
    Given the source table "<source_table>" contains duplicate rows (all columns identical except Filler_1)
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then all rows where Filler_1 IS NOT NULL are cloned, including duplicates

    Examples:
      | source_table        |
      | ods_free_drug       |
      | ods_non_contracting |
      | ods_copay           |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Data type mismatch in other columns
    Given the source table "<source_table>" has a column <col> with type <actual_type> instead of <expected_type>
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then an error is raised with message "Column '<col>' in <source_table> must be of type <expected_type>, found <actual_type>"

    Examples:
      | source_table        | col            | actual_type | expected_type |
      | ods_free_drug       | Quantity       | string      | bigint        |
      | ods_non_contracting | Units_Provided | string      | bigint        |
      | ods_copay           | Copay_Amount   | string      | bigint        |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Missing required columns in source table
    Given the source table "<source_table>" is missing required column <col>
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then an error is raised with message "Source table <source_table> missing required column '<col>'"

    Examples:
      | source_table        | col            |
      | ods_free_drug       | Drug_Name      |
      | ods_non_contracting | Facility       |
      | ods_copay           | NDC            |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Extra columns in source table
    Given the source table "<source_table>" has extra column <extra_col>
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then the extra column <extra_col> is ignored in the clone table

    Examples:
      | source_table        | extra_col      |
      | ods_free_drug       | Extra_Column_1 |
      | ods_non_contracting | Extra_Column_2 |
      | ods_copay           | Extra_Column_3 |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Attempt to create clone table when it already exists
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" already exists
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then the clone table "<clone_table>" is dropped before creation

    Examples:
      | clone_table                |
      | ods_free_drug_clone        |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone  |
      | ods_copay_clone            |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Attempt to create clone table with incorrect NOT NULL constraint
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" is created with DELETE_FLAG as nullable
    When the clone process is validated
    Then an error is raised with message "DELETE_FLAG column must be defined as NOT NULL in <clone_table>"

    Examples:
      | clone_table                |
      | ods_free_drug_clone        |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone  |
      | ods_copay_clone            |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Attempt to clone from non-existent source table
    Given the source table "<source_table>" does not exist
    When the clone process is initiated
    Then an error is raised with message "Source table <source_table> does not exist"

    Examples:
      | source_table        |
      | ods_free_drug       |
      | ods_non_contracting |
      | ods_copay           |

# END
